# Three programs read settings like these: the web app (first part), the worker, which
# shares most of the web app's (second part), and the live stat tracker (third part).
# Copy this file to .env (which is never committed) and fill in what you need. The
# tests never read .env.
#
# The web app and the worker name their database PLATFORM_DATABASE_URL; the tracker's
# is DATABASE_URL. The names differ on purpose (R8), so a .env made for the tracker can
# never point the web app or the worker at the tracker's database, and the other way
# round. npm run dev:stats, stats:db-check and stats:copy read .env too.

# --- Web app -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every setting the web app reads (apps/web/src/server/config-schema.ts).
# All values below are made up.
# Lines marked SECRET must never be committed with real values; real ones live in the
# hosting provider's secret store, different in every environment (T-30).
# The app refuses to start if a setting it needs is missing, or any setting given is
# invalid. For local work, the lines that are not commented out are all it needs.

# local, test, staging or production
APP_ENV=local
PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
# optional: debug, info, warn or error (default info)
LOG_LEVEL=info
# none, one or cloudflare. Optional in local and test (default none); REQUIRED in staging
# and production, where the app refuses to start without it. "one" only when exactly one
# proxy of the host stands in front of the app and appends the address it was reached
# from; the sign-in attempt limits then count per visitor network. "cloudflare" when
# Cloudflare stands in front of that one proxy (Render): the visitor is the address in
# Cloudflare's CF-Connecting-IP, believed only on a request that reached the host from one
# of Cloudflare's addresses (record 081). With "none" every visitor shares one address,
# so one person's wrong guesses can lock out everyone.
TRUSTED_PROXY=none
EMAIL_FROM=hello@example.test
# optional, local and test only (refused anywhere else): what the web app runs on.
# stand-in (the default): made-up leagues and people in the app's memory.
# made-up-database: the made-up seed leagues in a database in memory, every migration
# applied; the areas not yet moved onto the database show an error page (record 055).
# LOCAL_DATA=made-up-database
# optional, local and test only (refused anywhere else), and only with
# LOCAL_DATA=made-up-database: on loads the seed's demo-shaped league (/larkvale) into the
# made-up database too, a whole season of a large league; it adds some seconds at start.
# LOCAL_DEMO_LEAGUE=on
# optional, local and test only (refused anywhere else), and only with
# LOCAL_DATA=made-up-database: a simulated league (/simulated) played from empty to its
# final tables at start, its size in `npm run simulate`'s words; on is 8 teams, 7 rounds.
# Above 30 teams the start takes about a minute.
# LOCAL_SIMULATED_LEAGUE="--teams 24 --divisions 4 --rounds 10 --tracked 6 --seed 7"
# optional, local and test only (refused anywhere else): the design the first made-up
# league of the stand-in is drawn under, for pictures of every page in every color set
# (node scripts/shots.mjs --design=<name>): crest, crest-light, midnight-gold, clean-court,
# or pine (a made-up green league's design, kept for pictures and tests).
# LOCAL_DESIGN=crest-light
# optional, local and test only (refused anywhere else): a UTC time the stand-in's made-up
# world starts its clock at, so a check can be run as if at that hour. Its clock then runs
# on from there. The made-up database keeps this computer's clock, so the app refuses to
# start with LOCAL_NOW and LOCAL_DATA=made-up-database together.
# LOCAL_NOW=2026-11-15T20:01:00Z
# optional, local and test only (refused anywhere else): the short name of a team of the
# first made-up league's current season, put in the bin with its games and results as the
# stand-in's world is made, as a team could be before A-17 (step 2.180), to see how every
# screen shows such a team. Only the stand-in's world reads it.
# LOCAL_BINNED_TEAM=badgers
# optional, local and test only (refused anywhere else): which bot check the sign-in forms
# draw (record 081). stand-in (the default) is a hidden field holding the answer that
# passes; made-up-turnstile draws Turnstile's own box from an address that does not exist,
# whose script a browser test serves itself (tests/browser/bot-check-box-test.mjs).
# LOCAL_BOT_CHECK=made-up-turnstile

# Staging and production only. Local work and tests never open a database or reach the
# sign-in service (T-201), so leave these out there.
# SECRET. REQUIRED in staging and production. Never the tracker's database: its login
# must be a member of app_user and of sign_in_store, not inherited (record 055).
# PLATFORM_DATABASE_URL=postgres://app:made-up-password@localhost:5432/league_local
# REQUIRED in staging and production: the Supabase project that signs people in.
# SUPABASE_URL=https://made-up-project.supabase.co
# SECRET. REQUIRED in staging and production.
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=made-up-supabase-key
# REQUIRED in production: Cloudflare Turnstile, the bot check in front of sign-in and
# sign-up (record 081). Its public site key, then its SECRET key. Staging takes both or
# neither: with neither the bot check is off, and start-up says so. Local work and tests
# use the stand-in whatever is given.
# TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=made-up-turnstile-site-key
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=made-up-turnstile-secret-key
# SECRET. REQUIRED in production only: elsewhere every email is captured (T-140).
# RESEND_API_KEY=made-up-resend-key

# Not used yet (R8): each becomes required with the step that first uses it. If given
# now, it is still checked.
# SECRET (at least 32 characters)
# SESSION_SECRET=made-up-session-secret-0123456789abcdef
# SECRET
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=made-up-stripe-key
# SECRET
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=made-up-webhook-key

# --- Worker --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# npm run start:worker reads APP_ENV, LOG_LEVEL, PLATFORM_DATABASE_URL, PUBLIC_BASE_URL,
# EMAIL_FROM and RESEND_API_KEY above, and the two below (apps/worker/src/config-schema.ts).
# In local and test it never opens PLATFORM_DATABASE_URL: it runs on a made-up database
# in memory. PLATFORM_DATABASE_URL is required in staging and production, RESEND_API_KEY
# in production only.
# On a hosted database its login must be a member of app_user and of queue_owner
# (record 053). The worker refuses to start if a setting is missing or invalid.

# optional: the port its health check listens on (default 3001; 0, any free port, only
# when APP_ENV is test)
# WORKER_HEALTH_PORT=3001
# optional, outside production: a folder each captured email is also written to
# EMAIL_CAPTURE_DIR=.local/captured-email

# --- Making a league -----------------------------------------------------------------
# npm run league:make uses the local test database in .local/seed-db unless it is given
# --hosted. With --hosted it reads MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL (the migration login: account
# rows and checks only) and PLATFORM_DATABASE_URL (the app's own login, which runs the
# commands), and refuses if this file names either: give them for that one command only
# (docs/operations/make-a-league.md). Use the test copy only, with made-up data; never
# production (T-201). So these stay commented out here.

# SECRET
# MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL=postgres://migrations:made-up-password@localhost:5432/league_local
# verify (default), no-verify or off; for a database not on this computer only verify,
# with the server's certificate file below
# MIGRATION_DATABASE_SSL=verify
# MIGRATION_DATABASE_CA=./made-up-ca.crt

# --- Live stat tracker ---------------------------------------------------------------
# npm run dev:stats, stats:db-check and stats:copy read these.

# Save to Supabase instead of this computer. In Supabase: Connect → Session pooler →
# copy the connection string and put your database password in place of [YOUR-PASSWORD].
# Check it with: npm run stats:db-check
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.abcdefghijklmnopqrst:your-database-password@aws-0-us-east-1.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres

# Optional: Supabase's SSL certificate (Database settings → SSL), as a file path, so the
# server's identity is verified as well as the connection encrypted.
# DATABASE_CA=./prod-ca-2021.crt

# Let phones on the same Wi-Fi watch live (and, with a passcode, score).
# LIVE_STATS_LAN=1
# LIVE_STATS_SCORER_PASSCODE=

# Online hosting only: see docs/operations/live-stats-hosting.md.
# LIVE_STATS_PUBLIC_URL=https://stats.example.org
